From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000 linux port <sf2000@local>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: enable MIPS bFLT LO16 fixup hook

The generic bFLT loader detects arch relocation helpers using preprocessor
hooks. The prior LO16 address-bound fixup was implemented as a plain inline
function named flat_reloc_addr_fixup(), so fs/binfmt_flat.c still installed
its fallback identity macro and the MIPS fixup never ran.

Expose the helper through the macro hook that binfmt_flat expects. This keeps
the generic bounds correction active for out-of-range LO16 reconstructions
without adding any BusyBox-specific special cases.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
@@ -183,7 +183,7 @@ static inline int flat_put_addr_at_rp(u32 __user *rp, u32 addr, u32 relval)
 	}
 }
 
-static inline u32 flat_reloc_addr_fixup(u32 relval, u32 addr, u32 limit)
+static inline u32 mips_flat_reloc_addr_fixup(u32 relval, u32 addr, u32 limit)
 {
 	if (flat_mips_reloc_type(relval) == FLAT_MIPS_R_LO16 &&
 	    addr > limit && addr >= 0x10000 && addr - 0x10000 <= limit)
@@ -192,6 +192,9 @@ static inline u32 mips_flat_reloc_addr_fixup(u32 relval, u32 addr, u32 limit)
 	return addr;
 }
 
+#define flat_reloc_addr_fixup(rel, addr, limit) \
+	mips_flat_reloc_addr_fixup(rel, addr, limit)
+
 /*
  * elf2flt stores the MIPS relocation kind in the top two bits. Keep the
  * remaining 30 bits for the relocation target offset.
-- 
